  "body": "The dev launcher runs `npm install` in `backend/` the first time a worktree is used, so the generated lockfile showed up as untracked noise in every new worktree.\n\nNothing consumes it: the Dockerfile installs backend deps with `npm install --omit=dev`, and only `frontend/package-lock.json` is tracked (used by its `npm ci`). So the file is ignored rather than committed, matching how the backend is actually installed today.\n\nThe stricter alternative — commit the lockfile and switch the Dockerfile to `npm ci --omit=dev` for reproducible backend installs — is a real improvement but a build-behavior change, so it's deliberately not bundled here.",
